<h1 class="page-title">About the .NET Regex Tester</h1>

<p>
    This is a free online tester for .NET regular expressions. Patterns run on the real
    <code>System.Text.RegularExpressions</code> engine from .NET, compiled to WebAssembly with Blazor,
    so the results match what your C# code will do.
</p>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">Your data stays in your browser</h2>
<p>
    All matching happens client-side. Your pattern and test text are never sent to a server. The app only
    remembers your last pattern, test strings and options in your browser's local storage.
</p>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">Features</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Highlighted matches, a match table and capture groups (including named groups)</li>
    <li>All <code>RegexOptions</code>: IgnoreCase, Multiline, Singleline, ExplicitCapture, IgnorePatternWhitespace,
        RightToLeft, CultureInvariant, ECMAScript, NonBacktracking and AnyNewLine</li>
    <li><code>Regex.Split</code> and <code>Regex.Replace</code> with substitutions such as <code>$1</code> and <code>${name}</code></li>
    <li>Sample patterns, and export of matches as JSON, CSV or text</li>
    <li>A 2-second match timeout that stops runaway patterns (catastrophic backtracking) instead of freezing the page</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">Hosting</h2>
<p>
    This app is hosted on a
    <a href="http://www.orangepi.org/html/hardWare/computerAndMicrocontrollers/details/Orange-Pi-Zero.html">tiny ARMv7 Linux server</a>
    with only 256 MB RAM. The pages are rendered to static HTML when the app is built, so the server only hands
    out files; all the regex work is done by your browser.
</p>

<p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="">Open the regex tester</a></p>
